Three libraries want the headers of the Active Template Library, which
are a part of Visual Studio that this machine does not have and that cannot
be written to.  The libraries are the embedding of objects, the accessibility
of Windows and the library beside it; the kernel of the documents needs none of
them.  They are built without sources, so that what is delivered is still
there.

